From a4e2041e3f076f96607431593902c0063435e6b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jerzy=20Ko=C5=82osowski?= <jerzy@kolosowscy.pl>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2025 13:38:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] Enhance Display Presets with monitor availability
 detection and improved UI

Monitor Availability Detection:
- Add isPresetAvailable() to check if all preset monitors are connected
- Add isOutputCurrentlyConnected() for individual monitor availability
- Gray out unavailable monitors individually instead of entire preset
- Disable Apply button only when entire preset is unavailable
- Show warning text when some monitors are unavailable

Monitor Information Enhancements:
- Display full monitor names (vendor + model) instead of port names
- Show monitor priority number in top-right corner instead of highlighting primary
- Add support for EDR policy alongside HDR indicators
- Always show scale information (not just when != 100%)
- Improve text layout with wrapping and larger fonts for better readability

Technical Improvements:
- Store monitor vendor, model, and connection state in preset JSON
- Add proper i18n support for all user-visible strings
- Remove debug console.log statements and excessive qDebug output
- Fix QML syntax errors (TextArea.Wrap -> Text.Wrap)
- Clean up code structure and error handling

UI Polish:
- Increase font sizes for resolution and scale information
- Better text wrapping for long monitor names
- Responsive layout that adapts to preview size
- Consistent color scheme for available/unavailable states
