From bc0911925588ad007039802bb0d5658b2837c28c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jerzy=20Ko=C5=82osowski?= <jerzy@kolosowscy.pl>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2025 15:16:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] Enhance Display Presets with editing functionality and
 improved UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Major improvements to the Display Presets feature:

## New Edit Functionality
- Added "Edit" button to preset list allowing name/description changes
- Implemented edit dialog with form fields for name and description
- Added renamePreset() and updatePresetDescription() methods to KCM and PresetManager
- Smart updating - only changes modified fields

## Improved Preset Loading
- Refactored loadPreset() to work through OutputModel for proper UI updates
- Removed problematic variantMapToConfig() method that caused config conflicts
- Preset loading now only updates UI, user must click Apply to activate
- Added updateLastUsed() method separate from full preset loading

## UI Enhancements
- Changed "Apply" button to "Load Preset" for clarity
- Enhanced HDR/EDR labels with capability checking and bold formatting
- Fixed EDR policy detection (policy=1 means Always enabled)
- Improved text rendering with proper Rich Text support

## Code Cleanup
- Removed unused loadPreset() method and variantMapToConfig() from PresetManager
- Removed presetLoaded signal (no longer needed)
- Cleaned up debug logging for production readiness
- Added proper OutputModel integration for reactive UI updates

## Architecture Improvements
- Separated preset data retrieval from UI updates
- Better separation between model updates and system application
- Consistent use of OutputModel::setData() for UI changes
- Proper signal emission for model updates

All preset operations now work correctly with the standard KDE workflow:
Load Preset → Review/Modify Settings → Apply Changes
