From d041a1b1ef3cc90bc5968642b5d6a8953886c670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jerzy=20Ko=C5=82osowski?= <jerzy@kolosowscy.pl>
Date: Tue, 16 Sep 2025 14:23:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] Refactor preset architecture to move functionality from
 plasmoid to KDED daemon

- Move PresetApplier from plasmoid to kded/ for centralized preset management
- Add D-Bus interface methods (applyPreset, getPresets, isPresetAvailable, isPresetCurrent) to KScreenDaemon
- Integrate PresetModel in plasmoid to communicate via D-Bus with daemon
- Simplify PresetApplier with helper methods (buildPresetOutputsMap, applyPresetToOutput)
- Add keyboard shortcut support to preset structure (ShortcutRole)
- Clean up code by removing duplicate implementations and unnecessary debug logging
- Update plasmoid PresetList.qml to use model.isCurrent directly for status indication
- Fix primary output assignment to use 'primary' boolean instead of priority == 1
- Add missing KF6::GlobalAccel dependency for future shortcut functionality

This refactoring improves separation of concerns: daemon handles preset logic while
plasmoid provides UI, communicating through well-defined D-Bus interface.
